# Alembic autogenerated versions — we keep committed migrations only
# alembic/versions/tmp_*.py

# Output of `scripts/measure_surface.py`. Deliberately not committed: it is a
# measurement of the working tree, so a stale copy in git would be a second
# source of truth for the numbers ARCHITECTURE.md §11 quotes — and the wrong
# one. Regenerate it instead of reading it.
surface.json

# Hypothesis's example database. It grows to hundreds of KB of failing-example
# cache and is machine-local by nature. Hypothesis writes a nested
# `.hypothesis/.gitignore` containing `*` on first run, so git already ignores
# it — this line is here so the exclusion is stated in one place we control
# rather than depending on a file a dependency happens to create.
.hypothesis/
